{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Source to Docs Sync",
  "description": "Monitors all source files in the repository (Dart, Go, JavaScript, shell scripts, and configuration files) and triggers documentation updates in README.md or docs/ folder when changes are detected",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "lib/**/*.dart",
      "cmd/**/*.go",
      "internal/**/*.go",
      "pkg/**/*.go",
      "bin/**/*.dart",
      "test/**/*.dart",
      "scripts/**/*.sh",
      "*.js",
      "*.ts",
      "*.yaml",
      "*.yml",
      "*.json",
      "pubspec.yaml",
      "go.mod",
      "Makefile",
      "analysis_options.yaml",
      ".flutter_keycheck.yaml"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Source code files have been modified in this Flutter KeyCheck project. Please analyze the changes and update the documentation accordingly. Focus on:\n\n1. If README.md exists, update it to reflect any new features, API changes, or usage patterns\n2. If there's a docs/ folder, update relevant documentation files there\n3. Pay special attention to:\n   - New CLI commands or options (lib/src/commands/)\n   - API changes in the main library (lib/flutter_keycheck.dart)\n   - New configuration options (.flutter_keycheck.yaml, pubspec.yaml)\n   - Build system changes (Makefile, go.mod)\n   - New test patterns or examples\n\nEnsure the documentation accurately reflects the current state of the codebase and maintains consistency with the project's enterprise-grade Flutter widget key analyzer positioning."
  }
}